  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the grill to high. Cut the bread rolls in half. Finely grate the parmesan. Drain and rinse the beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353061/photos/large/266472_1-8158fcf9a89688f5d7cbbb3a5f56de86.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook beans: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a small saucepan over medium-high heat. Add the beans, tomato paste, half the country seasoning, ½ tsp sugar and 60ml (¼ cup) water and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 3-4 mins until slightly reduced. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353063/photos/large/266472_2-850f5fbc8cd6dd7c50e02cbe4a9f9753.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast rolls: Meanwhile, put the rolls on an oven tray, cut-side up, and grill for 3-4 mins until toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353065/photos/large/266472_3-2c58eb29d3998115e8ac9b804a063ea5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dress salad leaves: Combine 2 tsp olive oil and 2 tsp white wine vinegar in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the salad leaves and toss to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353067/photos/large/266472_4-67748553711fa9d215a8955141720ff9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the rolls among plates, cut-side up. Spoon over the beans and scatter with the parmesan. Serve with the salad leaves and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353068/photos/large/266472_5-5ee6b0c70f3ef80250ea13bfc891742f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: If you like a kick of heat, scatter over a pinch of chilli flakes or thinly sliced fresh chilli just before serving.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2353070/photos/large/266472_6-6008943387a372362a097cc2b5e7fe2e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
